⛔ THE WEBSITE IS NOT A MAXON PROJECT, AND `maxon fmt` MUST NOT DESCEND INTO IT.

`fmt` with no path formats the whole current directory, and it prunes only directories holding `.git`.
While the site was its own checkout that was enough; inside this repository it is not, so without this
marker a root `maxon fmt` would rewrite `src/examples/*.maxon` in place and walk every directory under
`node_modules/` looking for files that are not there.

The marker is a FLAG — this text is never read by anything. See `Compiler.collectMaxonSources`.

⚠ It also means the site's example programs are NOT compiled or checked by this repository. They are
hand-synced copies of `examples/` (MAINTAINING.md, "Content sync") and drift whenever an example
changes without them; serving them from `examples/` would remove the second copy.
